kosha sodium

  -- Na. proton-11. period 3, group 1 alkali metal. valence: 1 (loses 1 electron).
  -- highly reactive — reacts violently with water: 2Na + 2H2O → 2NaOH + H2.
  -- in ionic form Na⁺: essential for nerve impulses, muscle contraction, osmosis.
  -- NaCl (table salt): Na⁺ + Cl⁻ — the most familiar ionic compound.
  -- sodium-vapour lamps: characteristic yellow light (589nm emission).

